{"name":"Country Summer","hex":"#fffbd7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"country","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The territory of a nation; a sovereign state or a region once independent and still distinct in institutions, language, etc. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A large area regarded as distinct from other areas, e.g. because it is inhabited by a specific group of people"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["From or in the countryside, connected with it, or typical of it.","Of or connected to country music."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/country"},{"term":"summer","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One of four seasons, traditionally the second, marked by the longest and typically hottest days of the year due to the inclination of the Earth and thermal lag. Typically regarded as spanning  either the period between the summer solstice to the autumnal equinox, or the months of June, July, and August in the Northern Hemisphere and the months of December, January and February in the Southern Hemisphere.","year; used to give the age of a person, usually a young one."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To spend the summer, as in a particular place on holiday."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/summer"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sonoma County, California","blocks":[{"text":"Sonoma County is a northern county in the U.S. state of California. As of the 2020 United States census, its population was 488,863. The county seat and the largest city in the county is Santa Rosa."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Sonomamtnvineyard.jpg/330px-Sonomamtnvineyard.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sonoma_County%2C_California"},{"title":"Country","blocks":[{"text":"A country is a political entity or its territory in the world. They function as sovereign states, unrecognized states, constituent countries, or dependent territories. A country may consist of multiple nations, a structure known as a multinational state. Countries are often distinguished as developing countries or developed countries. There is no universal agreement on the number of \"countries\" in the world. This ambiguity is a result of several countries not being recognized as sovereign states by the UN system, but are recognized by at least one UN member, known as \"diplomatic recognition\". These countries often have disputed territories and have only partial recognition. A number of entities without recognition are also commonly considered a country."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Official_United_Nations_World_Map_-_October_2022.svg/330px-Official_United_Nations_World_Map_-_October_2022.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Country"},{"title":"Summer","blocks":[{"text":"Summer or summertime is the hottest and brightest of the four temperate seasons, occurring after spring and before autumn. Starting on the summer solstice, daylight hours are the longest and darkness hours are the shortest, with day length decreasing as the season progresses after the solstice. In the Northern Hemisphere, summer is usually defined as starting on June 21 or 22, and ending on September 22 or 23; and in the Southern Hemisphere, as the period between December 22 or 23 and March 20 or 21."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c4/Field_Hamois_Belgium_Luc_Viatour.jpg/330px-Field_Hamois_Belgium_Luc_Viatour.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Summer"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Hotel_La_Rose%2C_5th_and_Wilson_Sts.%2C_Santa_Rosa%2C_CA_6-12-2010_8-14-50_PM.JPG/500px-Hotel_La_Rose%2C_5th_and_Wilson_Sts.%2C_Santa_Rosa%2C_CA_6-12-2010_8-14-50_PM.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Hotel_La_Rose%2C_5th_and_Wilson_Sts.%2C_Santa_Rosa%2C_CA_6-12-2010_8-14-50_PM.JPG/1280px-Hotel_La_Rose%2C_5th_and_Wilson_Sts.%2C_Santa_Rosa%2C_CA_6-12-2010_8-14-50_PM.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Hotel_La_Rose%2C_5th_and_Wilson_Sts.%2C_Santa_Rosa%2C_CA_6-12-2010_8-14-50_PM.JPG/500px-Hotel_La_Rose%2C_5th_and_Wilson_Sts.%2C_Santa_Rosa%2C_CA_6-12-2010_8-14-50_PM.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHotel_La_Rose%2C_5th_and_Wilson_Sts.%2C_Santa_Rosa%2C_CA_6-12-2010_8-14-50_PM.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Sonoma_City_Hall_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Sonoma_City_Hall_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Sonoma_City_Hall_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Sonoma_City_Hall_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/Sonoma_City_Hall_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Sonoma_City_Hall_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASonoma_City_Hall_(cropped).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Rancho_Petaluma_Adobe_-_2018_-_Stierch_01.jpg/500px-Rancho_Petaluma_Adobe_-_2018_-_Stierch_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/96/Rancho_Petaluma_Adobe_-_2018_-_Stierch_01.jpg/500px-Rancho_Petaluma_Adobe_-_2018_-_Stierch_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parse